URI- Uniform Resource Identifier

- A URI  is a string of character used to indentifiy a resource on the internet either by lcoation ,name or both
- It provides mechanism for accessing the representation of a resource over the netowrk, typically through 
  specific protocls such as https or https

- URI are a broad category that includes both URLS(Uniform Resource Locators) and URN( Uniform Resource Names)



Sub Resource;
- A sub resource is a resouce that is hierarhicaoly under another resourse
- its part of a larger resource and can be acessed by extending the URL  OF TH EPARENT RESOURCE
- Sub resources are often used in RESTful API to maintain a logical 
  hierarchi of data and to faciliate each access to related resources.

- Example- In a bloggin platform, you might have a users resources identified by a URI
  A speciific user could be a resource acessible at/users/{usersid}
- if each user can have blog posts, a post would be a sub-resource of that user,
